<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06GX">Remark <span data-tag="06GX">9.4.1.10</span>.</a> Let $\kappa \trianglelefteq \lambda $ be regular cardinals and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category. Then $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-compactly generated if and only if it is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-cocomplete and satisfies the following stronger version of condition $(b_{\kappa ,\lambda })$: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(b_{\kappa ,\lambda }^{+} )$</dt>
<dd><p>
Every object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ can be realized as the colimit of a diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(A) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\quad \quad (\alpha \in A) \mapsto \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{\alpha }, \]
</div>
<p>
 where $(A,\leq )$ is a $\lambda $-small $\kappa $-directed partially ordered set and each $C_{\alpha }$ is a $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-compact object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
<p> This follows from Theorem <a data-tag="02QA" href="/tag/02QA">9.1.8.7</a> (for the case $\kappa \triangleleft \lambda $) and Example <a data-tag="067A" href="/tag/067A">9.4.1.9</a> (for the case $\kappa = \lambda $). </p>
</article>
